2. Uses requiring a separate commercial license

Without that separate written authorization, you may not use, modify,
distribute or integrate the Software for commercial purposes, including:

(a) selling or licensing an application, charging for downloads, subscriptions,
    in-app purchases, premium features or access, or monetizing it through
    advertisements;
(b) incorporating, preinstalling or bundling it in robots, hardware, software
    or other products developed, offered or distributed for commercial benefit;
(c) using it internally for an enterprise's business operations, production,
    customer delivery or commercial product research and development, even
    when neither the Software nor access to it is sold separately;
(d) providing services based on the Software for a fee or other direct or
    indirect commercial benefit, including hosting, APIs, deployment,
    customization and support.

These restrictions apply to individuals and organizations, to original and
modified versions, and whether deployed on a phone, other device, on premises
or in the cloud. A single-user or single-tenant deployment is not exempt.
Free distribution or free access is not sufficient to make a commercial use
noncommercial. Conversely, multiple users or tenants alone do not make an
otherwise noncommercial use commercial. Keeping the original logo does not
authorize commercial use. The permission to charge for support or warranties
in section 9 of the incorporated Apache License 2.0 does not override these
commercial-use restrictions.

